!!id:"https://tson.io/2026/38/m/meta-kernel-resolved.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/2026/38/m/meta-kernel.tn"
@doc:"""
  Resolver-output fixture for meta-kernel.tn (2026 Revision 38 draft).
  Parse the source schema, run the resolver, canonicalise, compare.

  Conventions:
  - Fields at their default values are omitted (`optional: false`,
    `voidable: false`, `role: FREE`).
  - `type_definition.supertypes` and `subtypes` are complete and
    lexically sorted; a resolver's native ordering is
    implementation-defined, so comparison tools canonicalise both
    lists before comparing. Set-typed fields are compared as
    written, in source declaration order (Part 2 Sections 7.5, 8).
  - `record.supertypes` inside bodies preserves source order (it
    records what was written).
  - `subtypes` lists entries of this map only; inverse edges from
    schemas that import this one are not represented here.
  - Source annotations are preserved in their authored positions,
    except `@doc`: a conforming resolver carries every source @doc
    verbatim, and these fixtures, which exist to be compared, leave
    entry docs out and substitute this conventions note for the
    document-level one.
  - Reference-kind names at type positions are stated as written: a
    reference is a hop, not a rewrite, so a use site naming an alias
    names the alias. A processor collapses the chain when it compiles
    readers, after linking, not in resolved output.
  - Type-reference positions (`record_field.type`,
    `tuple_element.element_type`, `type_definition.source`, choice
    variant elements, and binding-record type slots) hold type_ref
    values; `name` is type_ref's only required field, so a bare name
    token is the positional form (Part 2 Section 5.6, general over
    schema-backed data) and a braced record appears only when
    `arguments` is present — which, in output, is only where an
    application is still open: template bodies and `source`
    provenance (Part 2 Section 8.1).
  - The container constructors carry no parameters: their type
    slots are plain required `type_ref`-typed fields, filled by the
    construction (or by a sugar form's desugaring) like any other
    required field. Within a template body `value` also carries a
    parameter, unlabelled: a token there is a parameter exactly when
    its text resolves into the enclosing entry's `parameters`
    (Part 2 Section 5.10's shadowing rule), and a closed entry has
    none for one to resolve into. A parametric `= P` or `~ P` fixes
    nothing until materialisation makes the value concrete, when the
    field takes the role its literal spelling has, FIXED or DEFAULT;
    its `optional` is the name's mark as written (Part 2 Section 5.7).
  - `arguments` elements are type_argument records: `{ name: ... }`
    is a reference — including, in template bodies, parameter
    references of either kind, read against `parameters` — and
    `{ value: ... }` is a concrete literal.
  - `supertypes` and `subtypes` are name-level indexes.
    `reference.target` is a `type_ref`, so an alias to an
    application states the arguments it binds; a declaration's
    provenance lives in `source`, which records the applied form.
  - Every open entry is written as the constructor application it
    denotes, `<params> !C core-value` — a record template as
    `!record`, a container as `!array`/`!map`/`!choice`, an alias as
    `!reference` — and its body is held unread until materialisation
    substitutes the parameters away. Closed definitions carry
    binding-record bodies headed by the applied constructor.
    Instantiation entries are internally named (implementation-
    chosen, non-normative); none appear here, as nothing in this
    schema applies a non-constructor template.
  - Synthetic entries — the closed forms the sugar lifts to (Part 2
    Section 5.3) — source the constructor they build, are referenced
    by the field that wrote the sugar, and carry the derived
    `@synthetic` marker at their schema-map keys (Part 2 Sections 6,
    8.2); on ingest the marker is discarded and recomputed. Their internal names here follow the
    convention `<constructor>_<operands>_xxhash`, where the trailing
    `xxhash` is a placeholder for a content hash of the resolved
    binding record: the *shape* of the data — one internally named,
    `@synthetic`-marked entry per distinct concrete form — is the
    conformance point; the hash spelling is an implementation's own
    business and the placeholder is deliberately not a real digest.
  - Bare parameter names (e.g. T) in bodies are read against the
    enclosing entry's `parameters` list.
  """
!schema {
  top => !type_definition {
    subtypes: [array atom choice data enum enum_type identifier_type integer_type iri_type map product record reference regex_type set_type sum template text_type tuple type value_type void_type]
    body: !record { fields: {} }
  }

  type => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [top]
    subtypes: [array atom choice enum enum_type identifier_type integer_type iri_type map product record regex_type set_type sum text_type tuple value_type void_type]
    body: !record { supertypes: [top]  fields: {} }
  }

  atom => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [top type]
    subtypes: [enum enum_type identifier_type integer_type iri_type regex_type text_type value_type void_type]
    body: !record { supertypes: [type]  fields: {} }
  }

  product => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [top type]
    subtypes: [array map record set_type tuple]
    body: !record { supertypes: [type]  fields: {
      access_pattern => !record_field { type: product_access_type }
      size_type      => !record_field { type: product_size_type }
    } }
  }

  sum => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [top type]
    subtypes: [choice]
    body: !record { supertypes: [type]  fields: {} }
  }

  data => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [top]
    body: !record { supertypes: [top]  fields: {} }
  }

  reference => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [top]
    body: !record { supertypes: [top]  fields: {
      target => !record_field { type: type_ref }
    } }
  }

  template_param => !type_definition {
    body: !record { fields: {
      name  => !record_field { type: param_name }
      type  => !record_field { type: type_ref }
      bound => !record_field { type: type_ref  optional: true }
    } }
  }

  template => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [top]
    body: !record { supertypes: [top]  fields: {
      parameters     => !record_field { type: array_template_param_xxhash }
      template       => !record_field { type: text }
      extension      => !record_field { type: record_extension_type  optional: true }
      discriminators => !record_field { type: array_text_1_xxhash  optional: true }
    } }
  }

  value_type => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [atom top type]
    body: !record { supertypes: [atom]  fields: {} }
  }

  value => !type_definition {
    source: value_type
    body: !value_type {}
  }

  void_type => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [atom top type]
    body: !record { supertypes: [atom]  fields: {} }
  }

  void => !type_definition {
    source: void_type
    body: !void_type {}
  }

  boolean => !type_definition {
    source: enum
    body: !enum { members: [true false] }
  }

  integer_size => !type_definition {
    body: !record { fields: {
      bits   => !record_field { type: non_negative_integer }
      signed => !record_field { type: boolean }
    } }
  }

  integer_type => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [atom top type]
    body: !record { supertypes: [atom]  fields: {
      size          => !record_field { type: integer_size  optional: true }
      min           => !record_field { type: integer  optional: true }
      exclusive_min => !record_field { type: integer  optional: true }
      max           => !record_field { type: integer  optional: true }
      exclusive_max => !record_field { type: integer  optional: true }
      multiple_of   => !record_field { type: non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      members       => !record_field { type: integer_member_set  optional: true }
    }
    groups: [
      !field_group { members: [[min] [exclusive_min]]  optional: true }
      !field_group { members: [[max] [exclusive_max]]  optional: true }
    ] }
  }

  integer => !type_definition {
    source: integer_type
    subtypes: [non_negative_integer]
    body: !integer_type {}
  }

  text_member_set => !type_definition {
    source: set_type
    body: !set_type { element_type: text  min_items: 1 }
  }

  text_type => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [atom top type]
    subtypes: [identifier_type iri_type regex_type]
    body: !record { supertypes: [atom]  fields: {
      min_length    => !record_field { type: non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_length    => !record_field { type: non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      length        => !record_field { type: non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      pattern       => !record_field { type: regex    optional: true }
      members       => !record_field { type: text_member_set  optional: true }
      normalization => !record_field { type: normalization  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: NONE }
    } }
  }

  text => !type_definition {
    source: text_type
    body: !text_type {}
  }

  atom_specification => !type_definition {
    subtypes: [identifier_type iri_type regex_type]
    body: !record { fields: {
      spec => !record_field { type: iri }
    } }
  }

  identifier_base => !type_definition {
    source: enum
    body: !enum { members: [XID ID ASCII NONE] }
  }

  normalization => !type_definition {
    source: enum
    body: !enum { members: [NONE NFC NFKC NFKC_CASEFOLD ASCII_CASEFOLD] }
  }

  identifier_type => !type_definition {
    supertypes: [atom atom_specification text_type top type]
    body: !record { supertypes: [text_type atom_specification]  fields: {
      min_length    => !record_field { type: non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      max_length    => !record_field { type: non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      length        => !record_field { type: non_negative_integer  optional: true }
      pattern       => !record_field { type: regex    optional: true }
      members       => !record_field { type: text_member_set  optional: true }
      normalization => !record_field { type: normalization  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: NFC }
      spec          => !record_field { type: iri   optional: true  role: FIXED  value: "https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr31/" }
      start         => !record_field { type: identifier_base  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: XID }
      continue      => !record_field { type: identifier_base  optional: true  role: DEFAULT  value: XID }
      start_add     => !record_field { type: text  optional: true }
      continue_add  => !record_field { type: text  optional: true }
      medial        => !record_field { type: text  optional: true }
      exclude       => !record_field { type: text  optional: true }
    } }
